# Access control. Written against the tree in TOPICS.md — restructuring topics
# means rewriting this file, not just renaming.
#
# Deny is the default: a user gets exactly what is listed here and nothing else.
#
# Pattern for adding a device: it may WRITE only its own subtree, and READ
# whatever it needs to react to. A sensor that can publish anywhere is a sensor
# that can lie about the rest of the lab.

# You, from cipher: mosquitto_sub -t '#' and anything else.
user admin
topic readwrite #

# MAGI's own telemetry and service state.
user magi
topic write magi/#
topic read #

# --- devices, as they arrive -------------------------------------------------
# H-05, the LED strip. It reports what it is showing; it does not report
# anything else. It subscribes broadly because reacting to the whole lab is
# its entire job.
#
# user esp32
# topic write magi/light/status
# topic write magi/light/state
# topic read #
